   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h2",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Common mistakes that let bats return",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Many repeat infestations happen because one or two things were missed during repair. Watch out for these pitfalls.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Rushed, temporary seals:",
      "marks": [
       "strong"
      ]
     },
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": " Glue or foam over a seam will lift or crumble and bats will find another opening.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Ignoring HVAC pathways:",
      "marks": [
       "strong"
      ]
     },
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": " Bats or contaminated dust that reach ducts can keep odors and spores cycling through living spaces even after the attic appears sealed.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Sealing at the wrong time:",
      "marks": [
       "strong"
      ]
     },
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": " Excluding a roost during maternity season can be unlawful and inhumane. It also traps young, which leads to continued noise and mess until the problem is resolved correctly.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Not documenting work:",
      "marks": [
       "strong"
      ]
     },
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": " Without photos and a clear scope, future buyers or insurers will question whether the problem was handled fully.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h2",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Preventing future entries: maintenance checklist",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "After a professional exclusion, these maintenance steps reduce the chance bats find new access.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Inspect flashing, soffits, and vent screens annually, especially after roof work.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Trim tree limbs that overhang or touch the roofline to prevent easy access and wind damage that creates gaps.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Install chimney caps and maintain vent covers to industry standards.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Document any roof or attic penetrations done by contractors and ensure sealed penetrations return to metal flashing and welded mesh where required.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": [],
    "listItem": "bullet",
    "level": 1
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h2",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h3",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "How did bats get into my house through such a small gap?",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Bats can fit through narrow openings because of their flexible shoulder joints and small body size. They find gaps at flashing seams, behind loose soffit panels, and where vent screens have corroded. A focused dusk watch for emergence is the most reliable way to locate the active access point.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h3",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Can I remove bats myself by sealing the hole at night?",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "No. Sealing a roost while bats are present risks trapping animals inside and may violate wildlife laws during maternity season. Untrained attempts also increase exposure to guano and bites. Use a qualified professional who schedules exclusion and follows local regulations.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h3",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Will sealing attic vents cause moisture or mold problems?",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Proper sealing should preserve attic ventilation. Problems arise when vents are blocked without replacing ventilation pathways. Ask the contractor to evaluate baffles and ridge or soffit ventilation as part of the exclusion scope so you do not trade one problem for another.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h3",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "How much does it cost to get bats out and clean up guano?",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Costs vary by colony size, roof complexity, and contamination. Spot exclusion for a vent can be a few hundred dollars, full attic exclusion a few thousand, and heavy sanitation with insulation replacement can rise to the mid five figures in extreme cases. Get written, line-item estimates and references to compare quotes accurately.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h3",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "What should I do if I find bat guano in the attic?",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Limit attic access and avoid disturbing the material. Contact a bat-removal professional to confirm active roosts and scope cleanup needs. For heavy contamination, professional HEPA vacuuming and negative-pressure containment protect occupants from inhaling spores.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "h2",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Conclusion",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   },
   {
    "_type": "block",
    "style": "normal",
    "children": [
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "Understanding ",
      "marks": []
     },
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": "how bats enter homes",
      "marks": [
       "strong"
      ]
     },
     {
      "_type": "span",
      "text": " is the first step to resolving an infestation safely and cost-effectively. Most bat problems begin at small gaps: soffits, vents, chimneys, and flashing seams. Document emergence, call a licensed technician for inspection, and insist on durable, metal-based exclusion and appropriate sanitation when guano is present. That sequence prevents return visits, protects your HVAC and insulation, and reduces health risk for your household.",
      "marks": []
     }
    ],
    "markDefs": []
   }
